code: 0
--- stdout
Read issues before working on them: board status, blockers, history, description, comments.

Prints per issue: state, board status and fields, the sprint (with
fields.sprint), milestone, labels, assignees, blockers both ways with
their board status, status history on the board, the description and the
latest comments, indented. Times are UTC.

A blocker is resolved, no longer blocking, when it is closed or its board
status is in statuses.resolved, here: Ready, Done.
Unresolved blockers are listed first; a blocker whose board status could
not be read counts as unresolved.

Folding, always with a note saying what is hidden:
  - the last 5 comments are printed; --comments N prints the last N,
    --comments all up to 100 (the most gh dojo reads);
  - a description is cut at 2000 characters, and the comments shown share
    1500 (200 to 600 each); --full prints them whole.
--brief prints three lines per issue (four when GitHub hid part of it):
title; state, status, sprint, milestone, labels, assignees; blockers and
counts.
It takes neither --comments nor --full.

Several numbers are read in one request (up to 20 issues per request).
A missing issue or a pull request number is reported after the others are
printed, with exit code 3.

Usage:
  gh dojo show <N>... [flags]

Examples:
  gh dojo show 42
  gh dojo show 42 43 57 --brief
  gh dojo show 42 --comments all

Flags:
      --brief            three lines per issue: no description, history or comments
      --comments N|all   how many of the latest comments to print, or all (up to 100) (default 5)
      --full             print descriptions and comments without cutting them
  -h, --help             help for show

Global Flags:
  -q, --jq expression       filter the JSON with a jq expression (implies --json)
      --json                print the result as JSON (schema_version 1); errors stay text on stderr
  -t, --template template   format the JSON with a Go template (implies --json)
--- stderr
